1 — Product purpose and acceptance philosophy
Position as Workforce Credential & Compliance Readiness (Agentic Employee Records as the product name): a governed operational layer that continuously identifies gaps, routes verification to accountable teams, supports employee remediation, records evidence and authorizations, and reconciles approved status with designated enterprise systems. Workday HCM remains authoritative for worker/person/job/organization data; authoritative licensing bodies or approved verification organizations remain authoritative for professional license status; clinical privileging and operational authorization remain with appropriately authorized organizational decision-makers.

The hero story must communicate: Detect -> Explain -> Escalate if clinical risk -> Request evidence -> Employee responds -> Verify through correct source -> Authorized human decision -> Re-evaluate all applicable requirements -> Close the specific issue -> Reconcile with HRMS -> Measure outcomes.

NEVER automatically interpret document upload as verified clinical licensure. NEVER automatically set an employee's overall compliance score to 100 after closing a single finding. NEVER have an AI agent authorize clinical duties or autonomously suspend employment. NEVER allow a general HR user to impersonate a medical approver. NEVER infer official regulation from an uploaded company policy without human review.
